# Cross-Platform Consistency

SwarSadhana ships as three apps from one repo:
- **Flutter** (iOS + Android): `lib/`, assets in `assets/`
- **Standalone web**: `web/` (HTML/JS/CSS, not Flutter-web)

## Shared Assets

- Tanpura MP3 drones live in `assets/audio/tanpura/` (Flutter) AND `web/assets/audio/tanpura/` (web).
- When adding/modifying audio assets, update BOTH locations.
- Run `diff <(ls assets/audio/tanpura/) <(ls web/assets/audio/tanpura/)` to verify parity.
- Document every audio asset in `assets/licenses.md`.

## Feature Parity

- Every user-facing feature must work on all three platforms.
- When implementing a feature, implement it in BOTH the Flutter code AND the web JS code.
- The swara look-ahead strip, tanpura controls, and exercise UI must behave consistently.

## Testing Checklist (run for every change)

1. `flutter analyze` — no new errors
2. `flutter test` — all tests pass
3. `flutter build ios --simulator --no-codesign` — iOS compiles
4. `flutter build apk --debug` — Android compiles
5. Serve `web/` locally and verify in browser

## Sound Engine Mapping

| Feature | Flutter (iOS/Android) | Web (standalone) |
|---------|----------------------|-----------------|
| Swar demo | `dart_melty_soundfont` + `harmonium.sf2` | WebAudioFont Accordion preset |
| Tanpura drone | Recorded MP3 loops via `flutter_soloud` | Recorded MP3 loops via Web Audio API |
| Tabla | Sample-based via `flutter_soloud` | Synthesized via Web Audio API |
